{
 "_about": "TRANSLATOR SHELF: Eden Paul (1865-1944) and Cedar Paul (1880-1972), who translated mostly as a pair: Stefan Zweig, Romain Rolland, Schnitzler's Casanova's Homecoming, Emil Ludwig's Napoleon and Diana, Loria's Karl Marx, and others. Printings before 1931 only. Their sexology translations are left out (see _excluded). US public domain. Added 2026-10-10 by lane C (round 24); Adam may veto. No uids minted. Round 132 (2026-10-23, vetoable) added fifteen archive.org books Gutenberg lacks: Emil Ludwig's Bismarck (1927), The Son of Man (1928) and On Mediterranean Shores (1929), Masaryk's The Spirit of Russia (1919, 2 vols), Michels's Political Parties (1915), Loria's The Economic Synthesis (1914), Ribbert's Heredity, Disease and Human Evolution (1918), Baudouin's Suggestion and Autosuggestion (1921) and Studies in Psychoanalysis (1922), Rathenau's In Days to Come (1921), Kolnai's Psychoanalysis and Sociology (1922), the Vaertings' The Dominant Sex (1923), Rosa Luxemburg's Letters from Prison (1923) and Stalin's Leninism (1928).",
